      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "In the right triangle $GHI,$ $∠G$ is a right angle, $GH=24,$ $HI=26$ and $GI=10.$ What is the value of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡I?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's draw the triangle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14237399/assets/1429b33d88f438268a4168f57ff1417586c74e2dd034ff6241e0d2fddb6146b2.png)\n\nWe compute the cosecant of the angle $I$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡I=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{opposite}}=\\frac{26}{24}=\\frac{13}{12}\n$$",
